      "created_at": "2025-12-27T07:52:08Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-12-27T07:52:08Z",
      "body": "@picnixz  hi there, this is actually not duplicated of https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/143199 as the affected function here should be `element_subscr()`(slice handling), not the one discussed in this issue.\n\nHere is my proposed fix by adding a NULL pointer check after the possible re-entrant operation.\n```\nstatic PyObject *\nelement_subscr(PyObject *op, PyObject *item)\n{\n    // ... (existing code) ...\n    else if (PySlice_Check(item)) {\n        // ...\n        if (!self->extra)\n            return PyList_New(0);\n\n        if (PySlice_Unpack(item, &start, &stop, &step) < 0) {\n            return NULL;\n        }\n\n        // fix added here\n        if (!self->extra) {\n            /* The slice argument evaluation (via __index__) may have cleared \n               the element (re-entrancy). If so, the element is now empty. */\n            return PyList_New(0);\n        }\n\n        slicelen = PySlice_AdjustIndices(self->extra->length, &start, &stop,\n                                         step);\n        // ...\n```\nI’m new to contributing to CPython but happy to work on the PR + a regression test if this direction makes sense. Please let me know what you’d like to see.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
